    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d975">

                <pb facs="1325" n="1315" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1315"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.0031/5–2245</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Soong</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant
                        Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clayton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                Francisco</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-05-25">May 25, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Clayton</hi>: I am in receipt of your two
                    letters of May 22, one concerning registration of American firms in
                        China,<anchor n="64" xml:id="d975-f1"/> and the <pb facs="1326" n="1316"
                        xml:id="pg1316"/> second concerning draft treaty of friendship and commerce
                    between China and the United States.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d975-f2"/> I also
                    have the enclosed copy of draft treaty and copy of memorandum to the Embassy at
                    Chungking for use in negotiating treaty.</p>
                <p>These are having my careful attention and I shall look forward to discussing them
                    with you and your staff when I return to Washington on my way home.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>T. V. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Soong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
